000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID.    ACCTUPD.
000300 AUTHOR.       R HALVORSEN.
000400 DATE-WRITTEN. 11/02/91.
000500*------------------------------------------------------------
000600* ACCTUPD - APPLY MAINTENANCE REQUESTS TO THE UPDATE CONTROL AREA.
000700* SEVERAL STATEMENTS HAVE THEIR OPERAND ON THE NEXT LINE (THE
000800* VERB ALONE ON ITS LINE), AS AN OLD LINE-EDITOR HABIT LEFT THEM.
000900*------------------------------------------------------------
001000 DATA DIVISION.
001100 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
001200 01  WS-UPD-CONTROL.
001300     COPY
001400         UPDCTL.
001500 01  WS-AUDIT-PGM           PIC X(8) VALUE 'ACCTAUD'.
001600 01  WS-MSG                 PIC X(40).
001700 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
001800 0000-MAIN.
001900     PERFORM 1000-OPEN
002000     PERFORM
002100         2000-APPLY-UPDATES
002200     IF UPD-COUNT > 9999
002300        GO TO
002400            9999-ABEND
002500     END-IF
002600     CALL
002700         'ACCTLOG' USING WS-MSG
002800     CALL
002900         WS-AUDIT-PGM USING WS-UPD-CONTROL
003000     PERFORM 9000-CLOSE
003100     GOBACK.
003200 1000-OPEN.
003300     MOVE 'ACCTUPD STARTED' TO WS-MSG
003400     DISPLAY WS-MSG.
003500 2000-APPLY-UPDATES.
003600     ADD 1 TO UPD-COUNT
003700     MOVE 'Y' TO UPD-FLAG.
003800 9000-CLOSE.
003900     MOVE 'ACCTUPD ENDED' TO WS-MSG
004000     DISPLAY WS-MSG.
004100 9999-ABEND.
004200     DISPLAY 'ACCTUPD UPDATE LIMIT EXCEEDED'
004300     MOVE 16 TO RETURN-CODE
004400     GOBACK.
